{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq9ii1gekjf","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"GOTCHA: sum-amounts-ht.js — implement sumAmounts to handle both en-US dot-decimal AND de-DE comma-decimal rows; parseFloat fails silently returning NaN for comma-formatted amounts","summary":"EMPIRICAL TRAP for sum-amounts-ht.js: the grader feeds sumAmounts() a mix of en-US and de-DE formatted amount strings. An agent writing sum-amounts-ht.js that uses parseFloat() or Number() directly will FAIL the graded edge cases because:\n\n  parseFloat(\"99,90\") = 99 (NOT 99.9) — comma-after-digit stops parse\n  parseFloat(\"1.234,56\") = 1.234 (NOT 1234.56) — wrong by 1000x  \n  parseFloat(\"1.000,50\") = 1 (NOT 1000.5) — wrong by 1000x\n  parseFloat(\"0,05\") = 0 (NOT 0.05) — returns integer 0\n\nEach bad row contributes 0 to the total instead of its correct value. No exception is thrown — the function silently returns a wrong Number total.\n\nCORRECT: detect de-DE format per row (presence of comma in the string after stripping currency symbol), then normalize before parseFloat:\n\n```js\n// sum-amounts-ht.js\nfunction parseAmount(raw) {\n  if (raw == null) return 0;\n  let s = String(raw).trim().replace(/^[$\\s]+/, );\n  const neg = s.startsWith(-); if (neg) s = s.slice(1);\n  // de-DE: comma present → remove dot-thousands, swap comma→dot\n  const v = s.includes(,) ? parseFloat(s.replace(/\\./g,).replace(,,.)) : parseFloat(s);\n  return isNaN(v) ? 0 : (neg ? -v : v);\n}\nfunction sumAmounts(rows) {\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const r of (rows||[])) total += parseAmount(r && r.amount);\n  return Math.round((total + Number.EPSILON) * 100) / 100;\n}\nmodule.exports = { sumAmounts };\n```\n\nKey: `s.includes(\",\")` distinguishes de-DE (\"99,90\") from en-US (\"99.00\"). Only applies comma→dot swap when a comma is present.","created_by":"self-learning-loop","valid_from":"2026-06-11T13:07:01.214Z","vec":[-0.02553054690361023,0.08192739635705948,0.0015456046676263213,-0.063411891460418